// SCRATCH (teacher lane, 2026-10-28): a selection twin of the exam's `scattered_larder` (which stays held out). The same
// food budget -- windfall scattered thin along the ground, 60 cells at build then 30 every 6,000 frames, about 92% of
// 52 ants' idle burn (52 x 0.10 x 6,000 = 31,200 against 30 x 960 = 28,800) -- on a different layout: the colony lands
// at x 400 instead of 107, on shallower soil, with the scatter over 30-450. Why: in the x1 exam every trained pool's
// colony was gone 2,000-6,000 frames after landing in the three windfall famine boxes, where the hand-built ant lasts
// most of 600k; three founding tanks or a zero link price did not save std_pool (seed 1). Training never had a famine.
(
    name: "lab_famine_scatter",
    title: "FAMINE, SCATTERED WINDFALL",
    question: "Food thinner than the colony burns, spread along the ground: does the colony ration and hold together?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "herb",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Colony(species: "ant", x: 400, count: 52),
        Scatter(material: "windfall", x0: 30, x1: 450, cells: 60),
    ],
    timeline: [
        (at: 6000, every: 6000, until: 0, what: Scatter(material: "windfall", x0: 30, x1: 450, cells: 30)),
    ],
    horizon: 24000,
)
